HST Office: more VBA syntax that stopped modules from compiling, from real files.

- If x Then: y: the colon read as the end of the line, so End If was missing.
- Optional w As Worksheet = Nothing.
- Friend Sub, Friend Function, Friend Property.
- Keywords as members of a Type (Type As String, Name As String).
- A variable called Name: Name.Delete, Name = x.
- AddressOf F compiles (value 0): it is only for Windows API calls, which do not run here.
- Dim a(2) As Range gives Nothing elements: no object is made, and no error when the class is no class.
- The status bar and caption of Application work while a file loads and macro functions in cells run; it crashed.

- Public Event X(...) and RaiseEvent X(...) did not compile, so such a class module, and New on it, failed in every macro that uses it (3% of files). The event's handlers run in the objects whose WithEvents variable holds the object.
- ThisWorkbook.Path & "\x" works on Linux and macOS: Open, Dir, Kill, Workbooks.Open, Documents.Open, SaveAs.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/vba-corpus/language_cases.py.
